criteria:
Inclusion criteria:
Clinically indicated transcatheter valve intervention due to severe aortic valve stenosis, severe mitral valve regurgitation, or at least moderate to severe tricuspid valve regurgitation;
Sufficient cognitive ability to complete the questionnaires with assistance;
Ability for a telephone 6-week follow-up.
Exclusion criteria:
Any condition of impaired cognition that restricts the independent completion of questionnaires or the ability to report current symptoms;
Other conditions that make adequate patient information or consent to participate in the study impossible;
Valvuloplasty without planned valve implantation;
Interventional mitral or tricuspid valve replacement;
Other rare, interventionally treatable valve diseases (aortic valve regurgitation, mitral valve stenosis, tricuspid valve stenosis);
Inability to conduct a telephone follow-up six weeks after the valve intervention.
